Culture, society and technology - CST4

Modules covered What I will develop ….

Analytical geometry
Statistics
Similar and isometric figures
Functions
Trigonometry

➢ Ability to solve concrete, practical mathematical problems that are useful on a daily basis;

➢ Use my time effectively to understand the different concepts;

Course aimed at students who demonstrate an interest in the fields of
education, helping relationships, law, politics, the arts or communications. Page Number: 6 
6 

Natural Sciences - SN4 

Modules covered What I will develop …. 

Exponents and radicals 
Factorization 
The second-degree polynomial function 
The integer part function 
Analytical geometry 
Systems of equations 
Triangle trigonometry 
Statistics 
➢ Mastery of: 
• Exponent laws 
• Arithmetic and fractions 
• Algebra 
• Cartesian planes 

➢ The ability to develop proofs and demonstrations that 
call upon a good capacity for abstraction; 

➢ Maintaining a sustained pace in learning; 

➢ Understanding the origin and functioning of 
certain phenomena; 

Course aimed at students who are good at mathematics and 
demonstrating an interest in the fields of science, 
research or administration; 

JDLM requires a grade of 75% or more in 3rd secondary 
mathematics to access the SN4 sequence. 

